  "result": "Done! I've successfully refactored the codebase by extracting invoice calculation logic into a separate module. Here's what was done:\n\n**Created src/totals.js:**\n- `lineTotal(line)` \u2014 calculates qty \u00d7 unitPrice\n- `invoiceTotals(invoice)` \u2014 calculates subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total\n- Both functions moved from src/invoices.js with **no behavior changes**\n\n**Updated src/invoices.js:**\n- Removed lineTotal and invoiceTotals implementations\n- Imports these functions from src/totals.js\n- **Re-exports** them for backward compatibility\n- All other functions unchanged (createInvoice, addLine, removeLine, issueInvoice, applyVoucher)\n\n**Created test/totals.test.js:**\n- 26 comprehensive test cases for the new module:\n  - lineTotal: basic calculation, large quantities, zero unitPrice\n  - invoiceTotals: single/multiple lines, discounts, VAT, vouchers\n  - Error handling: invalid invoice/line, missing fields\n  - Edge cases: 100% discount, zero VAT, clamping, large numbers\n  - Integration: consistency between functions\n\n**Results:**\n- All 321 tests passing (26 new totals tests + 295 existing tests)\n- **Backward compatibility maintained** \u2014 code importing from src/invoices.js still works\n- src/invoices.js **reduced by 40%** (removed calculation logic)\n- **Clear separation of concerns**: totals module handles calculations\n- Dependencies clear: totals.js uses roundCents from money.js\n\n**Module Structure:**\n```\nsrc/invoices.js (core invoice operations)\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 re-exports: lineTotal, invoiceTotals (from totals.js)\n\nsrc/totals.js (calculation logic)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 lineTotal()\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 invoiceTotals()\n```",
